Building and running wincan
==============================

  ./configure            # finds cc, and x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc for the Windows window; see ./configure --help
  make                   # candled, and wincan.exe if MinGW-w64 was found
  make check             # the aggregation tests
  make install           # candled under $(prefix)/sbin, wincan.exe under $(prefix)/bin, the manual pages

The server runs on the machine that has the candle files (it needs only a C compiler and POSIX):

  make deploy HOST=name              # copies the sources there and builds candled
  ~/wincan/candled --dir /path/to/the/candles --port 8766
  ~/wincan/candled --dir /path/to/perp/candles --backfill /path/to/spot/candles    # perps first, spot for the time before they began

To start it at boot, copy contrib/candled.service to ~/.config/systemd/user/, set the directory in it, and
  systemctl --user daemon-reload && systemctl --user enable --now candled && loginctl enable-linger $USER

The window is one file, wincan.exe, with no installer and no dependency: copy it to the Windows machine and run it with
--server HOST:PORT once (the setting is then kept in %APPDATA%\wincan\wincan.ini).  The server's port must be reachable from
that machine.
